1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:02,697
{happy}Hello, and welcome to Shah Spectrum.

2
00:00:02,697 --> 00:00:04,730
If you're new here, welcome.

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:07,836
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us.

4
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:13,779
{happy}Imagine buying a share in a very well-known company, and then reading in its

5
00:00:13,779 --> 00:00:19,887
own paperwork that your vote will generally not change the outcome of any matter put

6
00:00:19,887 --> 00:00:20,849
to a vote.

7
00:00:20,849 --> 00:00:23,495
That is the deal in the Anthropic IPO.

8
00:00:23,495 --> 00:00:25,916
So what do its new shareholders actually own?

9
00:00:25,916 --> 00:00:27,135
{happy}I'm Mittal Shah.

10
00:00:27,135 --> 00:00:30,445
Come along, and we'll see who really holds the power here.

11
00:00:30,445 --> 00:00:31,463
{fluent}First, what happened.

12
00:00:31,463 --> 00:00:36,681
Anthropic, the maker of the Claude AI models, priced its IPO on the eighteenth of

13
00:00:36,681 --> 00:00:42,054
November at eighty-three dollars a share, and trading began on the Nasdaq exchange

14
00:00:42,054 --> 00:00:45,357
on the nineteenth, under the ticker A-N-T.

15
00:00:45,357 --> 00:00:52,260
An IPO, or initial public offering, is the first time a company sells its shares to

16
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,039
the public.

17
00:00:53,039 --> 00:00:57,635
We won't talk about the share price from here, because the interesting part is what

18
00:00:57,635 --> 00:00:59,071
those shares carry.

19
00:00:59,505 --> 00:01:03,645
Now, what does one of these shares give a shareholder?

20
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:07,022
Every share sold in the IPO is called Class A.

21
00:01:07,022 --> 00:01:11,593
It carries one vote, and it is an ordinary ownership stake.

22
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:12,494
That sounds simple.

23
00:01:12,494 --> 00:01:16,029
But the company has created other kinds of shares too, and they matter more.

24
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:18,805
First, the founders' share.

25
00:01:18,805 --> 00:01:23,922
One single share, called Class F, is held by a company set up by the seven

26
00:01:23,922 --> 00:01:24,573
co-founders.

27
00:01:24,573 --> 00:01:26,201
It has no share of the profits.

28
00:01:26,201 --> 00:01:31,966
But that one share alone carries fifty point one per cent of all the votes.

29
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:37,227
Reports on the filing say it ends once fewer than three of the seven founders remain

30
00:01:37,227 --> 00:01:38,566
in that company for ninety days.

31
00:01:38,809 --> 00:01:39,653
Second, the trust's share.

32
00:01:39,653 --> 00:01:45,014
Another single share, called Class T, is held by the Long-Term Benefit Trust, a

33
00:01:45,014 --> 00:01:47,355
group of independent trustees.

34
00:01:47,355 --> 00:01:53,145
Reports on the filing say that one share lets the trust choose a majority of the

35
00:01:53,145 --> 00:01:53,745
board.

36
00:01:53,386 --> 00:01:55,610
It also has no share of the profits, and no end date.

37
00:01:55,938 --> 00:01:58,716
So, what is left for the Class A shareholder?

38
00:01:58,716 --> 00:02:00,749
The filing answers in its own words.

39
00:02:00,749 --> 00:02:06,274
It says Class A shareholders, and I quote, "generally will not be able to affect the

40
00:02:06,274 --> 00:02:12,257
outcome of any matter submitted to a vote of our stockholders or the election of our

41
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:17,774
directors, regardless of how they vote." It adds that the structure may effectively

42
00:02:17,774 --> 00:02:25,258
remove their ability to influence major decisions, including a sale of the company.

43
00:02:25,658 --> 00:02:28,191
On the same thread, there is one more line.

44
00:02:28,191 --> 00:02:32,838
The filing says the founders' "personal economic interests in us will decrease while

45
00:02:32,838 --> 00:02:37,254
their voting control through the Founder LLC will remain unchanged."

46
00:02:37,622 --> 00:02:38,697
Finally, what do we not know?

47
00:02:38,697 --> 00:02:44,196
We have not seen how this structure is tested in practice, and we do not know if or

48
00:02:44,196 --> 00:02:46,007
when the founders' share will end.

49
00:02:46,007 --> 00:02:47,207
{happy}To sum up:

50
00:02:47,207 --> 00:02:51,244
the IPO gave the public a stake in Anthropic.

51
00:02:51,244 --> 00:02:53,130
It did not give them control.

52
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:56,782
Control sits in two shares that carry no share of the profits, and that is the real

53
00:02:56,782 --> 00:02:59,531
story behind the headline!

54
00:02:59,531 --> 00:03:03,812
{happy}This is news and explanation, not investment advice.

55
